Z||000000||Turkey on Rye||12-16-2001||08:48 PM||||Hi everyone, sorry we meet on unpleasant terms like this, but as the subject says, my car got jacked. Somejacka$$ backed out of his parking spot and tore the whole side of my car up. My mirror, trim, and custom scoop(the one from the fiero store)got broke off. Well i cant stand to see christina(my car) hurt like this, so i'm going to start the fixing process. I found a donor fiero for the trim, but how does the trim come off the door? Do you have to remove the door panel? And also, only of of the scoops is bad, is there anyone who has an extra one they might want to sell, cause i really dont wanna spend 300 bucks for two new scoops. Thank you for any help you guys may be able to give. This forum is wonderful. <BR>         Sincerely,<BR>                Chris ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Turkey on Rye||12-16-2001||09:05 PM||||"bumpity bump"||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||12-16-2001||09:27 PM||||Chris: Sorry to hear about your car.  Can't you let his insurance pay for it?  Anyway, the moulding is held onto the door by plastic clips.  You want to grab the bottom of the moulding with your thumbs and pull up.  The trim should pop off.  The clips will probably break in the process, so you will probably need those too.  Hope you can fix it up as good as new.  Good luck. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-16-2001||10:12 PM||||Rodney Dickman.com has the clips if you break em, also Kick Hill but they're SLOOOOW.<P>Rodney wil send them outlike that!<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">       <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed </FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
